5
00:00:13,094 --> 00:00:15,690
By the time the diagram is finished,

6
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:17,780
the path has already changed.

7
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:21,460
What if Claude ran the probes through code you

8
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,625
trust, read every hop as evidence,

9
00:00:23,625 --> 00:00:25,472
and drew the diagram for you,

10
00:00:25,472 --> 00:00:28,847
with a person approving before anything is published?

11
00:00:28,847 --> 00:00:31,649
That is traffic and flow diagram automation,

12
00:00:31,649 --> 00:00:33,560
done with Claude, done safely.

13
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:38,938
Gennoor Tech presents Traffic and Flow Diagram Automation with

14
00:00:38,938 --> 00:00:39,460
Claude.

15
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:42,912
One request in. One proven diagram out.

16
00:00:42,912 --> 00:00:46,098
Over three days you build a pipeline in eleven

17
00:00:46,098 --> 00:00:48,869
modules where Claude plans and explains,

18
00:00:48,869 --> 00:00:52,056
deterministic Python runs ping and traceroute,

19
00:00:52,056 --> 00:00:55,034
and every hop in the picture traces back to

20
00:00:55,034 --> 00:00:56,628
