21
00:00:56,628 --> 00:00:58,567
Claude never guesses a path.

22
00:00:58,567 --> 00:01:00,230
If a hop did not answer,

23
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:01,615
the diagram says so.

24
00:01:02,365 --> 00:01:05,995
You begin with what traceroute and ping can actually

25
00:01:05,995 --> 00:01:07,950
prove, and what they cannot.

26
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:12,347
Asymmetric return paths. Load balancers that hide pool members.

27
00:01:12,347 --> 00:01:14,302
Firewalls that drop I C M P.

28
00:01:14,302 --> 00:01:16,396
Then you set up the workbench.

29
00:01:16,396 --> 00:01:18,350
Claude Code on your machine,

30
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:20,654
the Claude Agent S D K in Python,

31
00:01:20,654 --> 00:01:23,237
and an M C P server that exposes only

32
00:01:23,237 --> 00:01:26,657
read only probe tools, with every call logged and

33
00:01:26,657 --> 00:01:29,100
credentials kept out of the prompt.

34
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:32,104
Next you build the probe runners.

35
00:01:32,104 --> 00:01:35,996
Deterministic Python wrappers around ping and traceroute,

36
00:01:35,996 --> 00:01:39,751
with timeouts, retries and parsers that turn raw output

37
00:01:39,751 --> 00:01:41,459
into a typed path record.

38
00:01:41,459 --> 00:01:45,283
Claude requests the probes through tool use and receives

39
00:01:45,283 --> 00:01:46,580
structured J S O N.

40
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:49,380
It cannot run a shell command on its own.

41
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:51,360
And when a hop returns stars,

42
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:54,774
the record marks it unknown instead of filling the

43
00:01:54,774 --> 00:01:55,047
gap.

44
00:01:55,797 --> 00:01:59,184
Day two adds context. Hops are enriched from F5

45
00:01:59,184 --> 00:02:01,634
through iControl REST and t m s h,

46
00:02:01,634 --> 00:02:04,948
from Citrix NetScaler through the NITRO A P I,

47
00:02:04,948 --> 00:02:07,903
